Abstract
The Hospital Management System (HMS) is a database-driven desktop application developed using Python, MySQL, MySQL Connector, and Matplotlib. The system automates routine hospital operations including patient registration, doctor management, appointment scheduling, billing, and report generation.
The application follows a modular architecture where each functionality is implemented in a separate Python module. Information is stored permanently in a MySQL database, making retrieval, updating, and reporting simple and efficient. Graphical reports provide a visual summary of hospital data such as patient distribution, appointment status, and billing statistics.
This project demonstrates the practical implementation of Python programming, SQL queries, database connectivity, modular programming, and exception handling in a real-world healthcare application. Such systems are commonly designed to reduce paperwork, improve data accuracy, and streamline hospital administration.
________________________________________
Introduction
Hospital management is one of the most important administrative activities in the healthcare sector. Hospitals maintain thousands of patient records, doctor profiles, appointment schedules, and billing details. Managing all these records manually is difficult, time-consuming, and prone to human errors.
The Hospital Management System is developed to replace manual record keeping with a computerized solution. The system stores all information in a centralized MySQL database and provides a simple menu-driven interface for performing operations. Every module of the application communicates directly with the database to insert, update, retrieve, or delete information.
The project is implemented using Python because of its simple syntax and powerful database libraries. MySQL provides secure and reliable data storage, while Matplotlib is used to generate graphical reports for hospital statistics. Together, these technologies provide an efficient and user-friendly hospital management solution.
