Conclusion
The Hospital Management System developed using Python and MySQL successfully automates the major activities performed in a hospital. The project demonstrates the use of modular programming, relational database management, SQL operations, and data visualization in a practical healthcare application.
The system effectively manages patient records, doctor information, appointment scheduling, billing operations, and graphical reporting. It reduces manual work, minimizes errors, and improves data organization. Although the application is designed as a desktop-based system, it provides a strong foundation for developing larger hospital information systems with advanced features such as authentication, cloud integration, and online services. Modern hospital management software typically evolves by adding these capabilities while retaining the same core modules of patient, doctor, appointment, and billing management.
