uture Improvements and Scope
The current Hospital Management System provides essential functionalities such as patient management, doctor management, appointment scheduling, billing management, and graphical reporting. However, there is significant scope for improving the system by adding advanced features that can make it more secure, scalable, and suitable for real-world hospital environments. Modern hospital management systems are increasingly moving toward integrated platforms with electronic records, analytics, cloud support, and patient-facing services.
1. User Authentication and Role-Based Access
Currently, the system directly provides access to all modules. In future, a secure login system can be implemented with different user roles:
•	Administrator Login
o	Manage doctors, patients, billing, and system settings.
o	Control access permissions.
•	Doctor Login
o	View assigned patients.
o	Check appointments.
o	Update medical records.
•	Receptionist Login
o	Register patients.
o	Schedule appointments.
o	Manage billing.
•	Patient Login
o	View appointments.
o	Check bills.
o	Access medical history.
Role-based authentication will improve data security and prevent unauthorized access.
